# Arteum 🎨

An Android app to explore and save artworks from the [Art Institute of Chicago](https://www.artic.edu/) public API.

---

## Features

- **Browse** a curated collection of artworks from the Art Institute of Chicago
- **Search** artworks by title in real time
- **Detail view** with full artwork info: artist, date, origin, medium and description
- **Favorites** — save and manage your favourite pieces locally
- **List / Grid** display mode toggle
- **Dark mode** support
- **Splash screen**

---

## Tech Stack

| Layer | Technology |
|---|---|
| Language | Kotlin |
| UI | Jetpack Compose |
| Navigation | Navigation3 |
| Networking | Retrofit + Gson |
| Image loading | Coil |
| Local storage | Room |
| Architecture | MVVM |
| Preferences | SharedPreferences |

---

## Architecture

```
com.example.apilistapp/
├── data/
│   ├── local/          # Room database, DAOs, entities
│   ├── mapper/         # DTO → Domain mappers
│   ├── preferences/    # Settings persistence
│   ├── remote/         # Retrofit API interface, DTOs
│   └── repository/     # Data repositories
├── domain/             # Domain models
├── ui/
│   ├── components/     # Reusable composables
│   ├── navigation/     # Routes, NavHost, BottomBar
│   ├── screens/        # detail / favorites / list / settings
│   └── theme/          # Colors, typography, theme
└── utils/              # Extension functions
```

---

## API

This app uses the **Art Institute of Chicago** public API — no API key required.

- Base URL: `https://api.artic.edu/api/v1/`
- Images: `https://www.artic.edu/iiif/2/{image_id}/full/843,/0/default.jpg`

---

## Getting Started

1. Clone the repository
```bash
git clone https://github.com/noagomigar/arteum.git
```
2. Open the project in **Android Studio Hedgehog** or later
3. Run on an emulator or physical device (API 26+)

No API keys or extra configuration needed.

